<!-- ===== CORE PRINCIPLES SECTION ===== -->
<section class="principles-section">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Core Principles</h2>
        <div class="principles-grid-8">
            <div class="principle-card-sm">
                <h3>Cataract Surgery</h3>
                <p>In the normal eye the lens inside is clear and transparent, but when cataract develops it becomes cloudy and opaque.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="principle-card-sm">
                <h3>Glaucoma</h3>
                <p>It's an eye disease that can cause blood vision. Often called as 'Sneak Thief Of Sight', Glaucoma is usually because there are no early warning signs.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="principle-card-sm">
                <h3>OptiLasik</h3>
                <p>It brings the procedure that comes to the shape of the cornea, mimicking the light falling on the cornea to properly reach the retina, thus improving the vision and reducing dependency on glasses or contact lenses.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="principle-card-sm">
                <h3>Bladeless Lasik Surgery</h3>
                <p>No matter how easily you are for a life without spectacles or contact lenses, the decision to have Lasik is a big one.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="principle-card-sm">
                <h3>Perimetry</h3>
                <p>We're pleased to announce the recent acquisition of state-of-the-art, high precision equipment at Eye Care Hospital.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="principle-card-sm">
                <h3>Floaters and Flashes</h3>
                <p>People may observe tiny moving spots or sudden bursts of light (flashes) in their vision. While these occurrences can be bothersome, they are typically not significant in terms of overall eye health.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="principle-card-sm">
                <h3>Yag Laser</h3>
                <p>A laser from A-Laser precisely focuses on the lens or the thick, molecular lens membranes, creating smooth, controlled openings of the desired size, without the impacting other delicate eye structures.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="principle-card-sm">
                <h3>Contact Lenses</h3>
                <p>Small visual devices, crafted from curved glass to match the eye's front curve, offer an artificial refractive surface. They are employed for correcting vision issues such as myopia and hyperopia.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

